      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/answer.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d12">180</data>
      <data key="d13">206</data>
      <data key="d14">def _writer(out=None):</data>
      <data key="d15">A write callable that cannot raise UnicodeEncodeError.

    The Windows console is cp1252: a single non-ASCII token from a model would
    otherwise abort the whole answer mid-sentence. Bytes go straight to
    sys.stdout.buffer when there is one; a text stream gets its input folded to
    what its own encoding can represent first.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3022.68" y="4194.83" width="74.75" height="29.90" />
